getHeader:
----------
In SAP Cloud Platform Integration (CPI), the getHeader function is a standard function used in message
mappings to retrieve the value of a specific header from the message. It's available as a built-in
function, allowing users to access header values without needing custom Groovy scripts. This function
is crucial for accessing information passed within the message header, which can influence the
integration flow or be used in data transformations.

Cloud Integration – Message Mapping – getHeader and ...

Here's a more detailed explanation:

Purpose:
The getHeader function retrieves the value of a header based on its name. Headers are key-value
pairs that can carry metadata or control information related to the message.

Availability:
Since version 6.46.34, getHeader is a standard function in SAP CPI, eliminating the need for
custom scripts in many cases, according to www.sprintegrate.com.

Usage:
In message mapping, you can find and use getHeader under the "Functions" tab when defining mapping expressions.

Example:
If you need to access the "Content-Type" header, you would use getHeader("Content-Type").

Null Handling:
If the specified header doesn't exist, the getHeader function will return "null", which you may
need to handle in your mapping logic (e.g., by setting a default value or performing other actions).

